To add SoundCloud music playback to your website, you'll need to use the **SoundCloud oEmbed API** or **JavaScript API**. The simplest approach is embedding tracks using iframes. Here's a step-by-step guide:

---

### **1. Basic Embed (No API Code Required)**
You can embed tracks directly by copying the embed code from SoundCloud's website:
1. Go to a SoundCloud track.
2. Click the **Share** button → **Embed** tab.
3. Copy the iframe code and paste it into your HTML.

Example:
```html
<iframe width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no" 
  src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/TRACK_ID&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true">
</iframe>
```

Replace `TRACK_ID` with the actual track ID (e.g., `https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name` → the ID is in the URL).

---

### **2. Programmatic Embed (With JavaScript)**
If you want users to input a SoundCloud URL or track ID dynamically, use the [SoundCloud JavaScript SDK](https://developers.soundcloud.com/docs/api/html5-widget-api).

#### **Steps**:
1. **Include the SoundCloud API script**:
   ```html
   <script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>
   ```

2. **Create a container for the player**:
   ```html
   <div id="player"></div>
   ```

3. **Initialize the player with JavaScript**:
   ```javascript
   const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
   iframe.width = '100%';
   iframe.height = '166';
   iframe.src = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/TRACK_ID&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true`;
   iframe.frameBorder = '0';
   document.getElementById('player').appendChild(iframe);
   ```

4. **Control playback programmatically**:
   ```javascript
   const playerIframe = document.querySelector('#player iframe');
   const player = SC(playerIframe);

   // Play the track
   player.play();

   // Pause the track
   player.pause();
   ```

---

### **3. Fetching Track Info (Optional)**
To retrieve track metadata (e.g., title, artwork), use the [SoundCloud oEmbed API**:

```javascript
fetch(`https://soundcloud.com/oembed?format=json&url=https://soundcloud.com/ARTIST/TRACK`)
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => {
    console.log(data.title, data.thumbnail_url);
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error('Error fetching track info:', error);
  });
```

---

### **4. Server-Side Rendering (Optional)**
If you're using a backend (PHP, Node.js, etc.), you can resolve SoundCloud URLs to track IDs using the API:

```javascript
// Example using Node.js (requires `client-id` from SoundCloud Developer Portal)
const clientId = 'YOUR_CLIENT_ID'; // Get this from https://developers.soundcloud.com/
const url = 'https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name';

fetch(`https://api.soundcloud.com/resolve?url=${encodeURIComponent(url)}&client_id=${clientId}`)
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => {
    const trackId = data.id;
    // Use trackId to embed the player
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error('Error resolving track:', error);
  });
```

---

### **5. Security Considerations**
- Avoid using the **SoundCloud Legacy API** (deprecated) or exposing API keys publicly.
- If using server-side resolution, keep your `client_id` secret and never expose it in client-side code.
- Sanitize user inputs if allowing dynamic URL entry.

---

### **Example: Full Working Code**
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>SoundCloud Player</title>
</head>
<body>
  <input type="text" id="trackUrl" placeholder="Enter SoundCloud URL or Track ID" />
  <button id="loadTrack">Load Track</button>
  <div id="player"></div>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('loadTrack').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const urlInput = document.getElementById('trackUrl').value.trim();
      let iframeSrc;

      if (urlInput.startsWith('https://soundcloud.com/')) {
        // Use oEmbed API (replace with server-side resolution for production)
        fetch(`https://soundcloud.com/oembed?format=json&url=${encodeURIComponent(urlInput)}`)
          .then(response => response.json())
          .then(data => {
            // Extract track ID (requires parsing the URL)
            const trackUrl = data.html.split('tracks/')[1].split('&')[0];
            createPlayer(trackUrl);
          })
          .catch(error => alert('Error loading track.'));
      } else if (/^\d+$/.test(urlInput)) {
        // If input is a numeric track ID
        createPlayer(urlInput);
      } else {
        alert('Invalid SoundCloud URL or Track ID.');
      }
    });

    function createPlayer(trackId) {
      const playerDiv = document.getElementById('player');
      playerDiv.innerHTML = `
        <iframe width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no" 
          src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/${trackId}&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false">
        </iframe>
      `;
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### **Requirements**
- A **SoundCloud account** (free tier works for basic embedding).
- Optional: Register as a developer to use the API at [SoundCloud Developers](https://developers.soundcloud.com/).

