To implement a typing animation effect in forms, I'll create a solution using CSS animations and JavaScript. This approach provides visual feedback during form interactions:

```css
/* Typing animation styles */
@keyframes typing {
  0% { width: 0; }
  25% { width: 3px; }
  50% { width: 0; }
  75% { width: 3px; }
  100% { width: 0; }
}

@keyframes blink {
  50% { border-color: transparent; }
}

.form-input:focus + .typing-cursor,
.form-textarea:focus + .typing-cursor {
  display: inline-block;
  animation: typing 1s steps(2, end) infinite, 
             blink 0.7s step-end infinite;
}

.typing-cursor {
  display: none;
  width: 3px;
  height: 1.2em;
  background-color: #3b82f6;
  margin-left: 2px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  border-radius: 1px;
}
```

```html
<!-- Example form with typing indicator -->
<form class="enhanced-form">
  <div class="form-group">
    <label for="name">Name:</label>
    <input type="text" id="name" class="form-input">
    <span class="typing-cursor"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label for="email">Email:</label>
    <input type="email" id="email" class="form-input">
    <span class="typing-cursor"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label for="message">Message:</label>
    <textarea id="message" class="form-textarea" rows="4"></textarea>
    <span class="typing-cursor"></span>
  </div>
</form>
```

For more advanced scenarios like simulating real-time typing in chat-style inputs, you can use this JavaScript approach:

```javascript
// For auto-typing simulation (e.g., placeholder text)
function simulateTyping(inputElement, text, speed = 100) {
  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    let i = 0;

    const type = () => {
      if (i < text.length) {
        inputElement.value += text.charAt(i);
        i++;
        setTimeout(type, speed);
      } else {
        resolve();
      }
    };

    type();
  });
}
```

Key considerations:
- The CSS-only solution is lightweight and works without JavaScript
- Place `.typing-cursor` immediately after each input in the DOM
- Animations trigger only when inputs are focused
- Adjust colors (`#3b82f6` blue shown) to match your design
- Modify animation speed (`1s`/`0.7s`) as needed
- Add `pointer-events: none` to `.typing-cursor` if needed

For performance:
- Use hardware-accelerated properties where possible
- Keep animations short to avoid distraction
- Ensure accessibility compliance (consider prefers-reduced-motion)
- Test across different browsers for compatibility

This implementation provides immediate visual feedback when users interact with form elements, improving perceived responsiveness and engagement.

