To reverse the short link back to its original long link, you can make a call to the short link service provider. Here's an example:

```javascript
// JavaScript code
const fetch = require('node-fetch');

const shortUrl = 'https://short.ly/abc123';

fetch(`https://short.ly/api/expand?url=${encodeURIComponent(shortUrl)}`)
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => {
    console.log('The original long URL is:', data.longUrl);
    // The original long URL is: https://www.coursera.org/specializations/cybersecurity
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error('An error occurred when parsing the short link:', error);
  });
```

Please replace `https://short.ly/api/expand` with the actual API address provided by the short link service provider. Some short link services may require additional parameters (such as API keys) to be passed in.

